      "parent": "ch_7",
      "parentHint": "Chapter VII",
      "sourceAnchors": [
        {
          "exactQuote": "30. ( 1 ) An order passed by the Appellate Tribunal under this Act shall be executable by it as a decree of civil court, and for this purpose, the Appellate Tribunal shall have all the powers of a civil court.",
          "occurrence": 0,
          "sourceId": "src:371"
        },
        {
          "exactQuote": "( 2 ) Notwithstanding anything contained in sub-section ( 1 ), the Appellate Tribunal may transmit any order made by it to a civil court having local jurisdiction and such civil court shall execute the order as if it were a decree made by that court.",
          "occurrence": 0,
          "sourceId": "src:372"
        }
      ],
      "titleAnchor": {
        "exactQuote": "Orders passed by Appellate Tribunal  to  be executable  as decree.",
